{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/init()"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/boundEvents"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/fallback(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/handler()","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(_:_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(eventNamed:_:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for three events opens with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event.event"},{"type":"text","text":", and that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"default:"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allow"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reactor handler is an "},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure, and collecting "},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" members by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at compile time, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trade for the same reason."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}]},{"text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signs no reply and interprets no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout_ms"},{"text":"; its output is exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/document